              "text": "گوردوارہ (gurdvārā) is \"the guru's gateway\", the Sikh place of worship. It joins Sanskrit guru, \"teacher\", and dvārā, \"door, gateway\", from Sanskrit dvāra, \"door\"; CDIAL lists the inherited Hindi duār under a form duvāra (CDIAL 6459)."
